Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||10-05-2001||10:08 AM||||Oh yeah, he also posted this a few days ago...<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>that'd be me... <A HREF="http://www.nitrouswarehouse.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrouswarehouse.com</A>  talk to john stewart he'll set you up... start with their nitrous jetting suggestions... then use jetting 52/22 you'll understand once you have the kit AND HANG THE HELL ON! it's under $500 and takes about 6 hours to install, with hiding all the wires and making it look nice. only use 93 octane and get new plugs, an MSD box and a decent coil. and you'll be FOGGIN up the city! oh buy stock in a tire company...  <BR>--- oh yeah... <BR>#20216 - GM/Fiero V-6 (50-75/hp, all jets included) complete with 10lb bottle (Upgrade 10lb bottle to 15lb bottle...add $60.00), nut/nipple, set steel hinged bottle brackets w/bolts, 16ft nitrous line, nitrous filter, set nitrous/fuel solenoids, set solenoid mounting brackets w/ screws, (2) 18" (1ea. red & blue) braided lines, (1) fuel rail connector line w/adapter, jets & jetting depending on the application, Shark Nozzle w/fittings (U.S. Patent# 5699776), air intake nozzle mounting bong, WOT throttle switch, lighted arming switch, 60 amp heavy duty anti-flyback relay w/wiring harness, misc. fittings & wiring for installation, set decals, & easy-to-follow complete installation instructions. This is a "wet" nitrous system (there's not a "dry" kit made that can run with an NX "wet" system), with no "retarded timing" (so the nitrous won't hurt parts and you have FULL engine power), and the fuel is taken off the fuel-rail at the "schrader valve", using your stock fuel pressure psi. This system doesn't require an extra fuel pump, nor is it necessary<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>||||reg||1
